    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Ten requests reuse the same prompt, and SGLang's radix cache serves requests 2-10 from the cached prefix (TTFT p50 337 ms), so the aggregate prefill_tok_s (6635) is cache-inflated. The cold single-request rate is the first request: 40,293 tokens in 19.5 s = ~2,070 tok/s. Decode figures on this row come from 5-6 output tokens per request and are not meaningful."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "link": "https://github.com/pangoleen/qwen3.8-27b-dgx-spark-dflash2",
      "text": "Served with the pangoleen DGX Spark DFlash2 recipe at master bac473f, exactly as its serve.sh defaults (no flag changed): target RadixArk/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4 554ebba9, DFlash2 drafter maurienne-ai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2-NVFP4-RTNcal bd7a9342 with 16 draft tokens, bf16 KV and mamba state, context 262144, mem-fraction 0.65, max-running 4, prefill CUDA graph disabled, FlashInfer autotune with the recipe-shipped tactic cache mounted, container pinned to cpuset 5-9,15-19. The image qwen38-27b-sglang-dflash2-sm121:0.3.0 was built on the host from the pinned base lmsysorg/sglang:qwen38-27b@sha256:3c0abdf4 plus the recipe's python overlay; engine.build names the recipe commit because the SGLang dev version string alone does not describe the served build."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Thinking is OFF in every row: the recipe passes --default-chat-template-kwargs {\"enable_thinking\": false, \"preserve_thinking\": false} and the packets send no override. Rows from thinking-on configurations of this model are a different config_id and are not decode-comparable with these."
    },
    {
      "severity": "info",
      "text": "Offline reproduction note: SGLang resolves the DFlash drafter's config through the speculative-algorithm alias hook without the pinned --speculative-draft-model-revision, so a HuggingFace cache filled by a revision-pinned download (which writes the snapshot but no refs/main) fails the offline lookup and the container crash-loops at startup. Writing refs/main with the pinned snapshot sha for both the target and the drafter repositories fixes it; the served snapshots are still the pinned revisions."
    }
  ],
